# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() stops a sleeping strand tagged with that tag;
#         concurrent variants: stop before vs after strand starts sleeping.
# blocked: parse error — `&` separator inside tag-scope block body not supported:
#   `tag: { {expr} & stmt }` → "<stdin>:1:N: expected '}'" (T39 reason stale)
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason (updated v0.13.4 probe):
#   OP_FORK_JOIN transient-strand guard removed (LANG-S06); tag.stop() method
#   dispatch has been available since M4.  The current blocker is a parse
#   error: the parser sees `{sleep(100ms); echo("No")} & tag.stop()` inside
#   the outer tag-scope body block and rejects `&` at the separator position
#   ("expected '}'").  The `&` statement-separator is not currently recognized
#   inside a `tag: { ... }` scope body at this parse level.
#
# Original urbiscript (re-activate when & inside tag-scope body parses):
# # var tag = Tag.new() | {};
# # tag: { {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} & tag.stop() };
# # tag: { tag.stop() & {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} };
